WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:04.036
-NBC held the third Republican
presidential debate last week,

00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:05.838
but there's still
some important questions

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:07.574
that have gone unanswered.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.742
So we decided to hold
a debate of our own.

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.911
That's right.
All five candidates

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.947
are right here, right now,
and they're ready to go.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.249
So without further ado,
here is the "Late Night"

00:00:17.249 --> 00:00:19.886
Republican presidential debate!

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:21.988
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:26.325
♪♪

00:00:26.325 --> 00:00:28.294 line:0%
[ Crowd murmuring ]

00:00:32.531 --> 00:00:35.168
Welcome to "Late Night's"

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:38.204
first 2024 Republican
presidential debate.

00:00:38.204 --> 00:00:41.341
I'm your moderator, Seth Meyers.
Let's jump right in.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:44.510
Ambassador Haley, what was
the most surprising thing

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:48.113
you learned during your time
as an ambassador to the UN?

00:00:48.113 --> 00:00:49.582 line:0%
-China is real.

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:50.817
-Oh.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.052
[ Laughter ]

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:55.722
Governor DeSantis, what is
your biggest accomplishment

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:57.257
as governor of Florida?

00:00:57.257 --> 00:00:59.592
-A significant decline
in life expectancy.

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:01.727
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.962 --> 00:01:07.500
-Mr. Ramaswamy, you said,
if elected, you'd ban Elmo. Why?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.802
-He's a puppet
for the managerial class!

00:01:09.802 --> 00:01:11.171
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.938 --> 00:01:15.374
-Governor Christie,
how would you describe yourself

00:01:15.374 --> 00:01:16.909
on this stage tonight?

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:19.212
-One of the big failings
among many.

00:01:21.414 --> 00:01:25.685
-Senator Scott -- Wait. Didn't
you drop out over the weekend?

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:26.886
What are you doing here?

00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:29.923
-If you're able-bodied
in America, you work.

00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:33.960
-You know you're still
a sitting senator, right?

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:42.801
-Mr. Ramaswamy, what does
"The New York Times" use

00:01:42.801 --> 00:01:44.270
to print their newspaper?

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:45.404
-Woke Inc.

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:47.306
-Boo! Boo!

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.208
-Let's not do this.
Let's not do this.

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.576
Let's let the candidates speak.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:54.513
-Hey, you moderate
the debate your way, Lester!

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:56.516
And I'll moderate it mine! Boo!

00:01:58.551 --> 00:02:02.955
Governor Christie, moving on,
you are a board-game enthusiast.

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.858
What's your strategy when
you play the game Battleship?

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:08.861
-The submarines are the single
most important thing.

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:10.630
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.998 --> 00:02:16.336
-Ambassador Haley, it's time
for our music trivia round.

00:02:16.336 --> 00:02:17.669
Answer this correctly,
and you'll get

00:02:17.669 --> 00:02:19.605
five points in the polls.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:23.375
Who sang the classic
R&amp;B hit "September"?

00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:24.844
-Land, Air and Sea.

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.179
-Mnh.

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:29.515
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:30.950
You know what?
It's close enough.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:34.286
-Thank you.
-You're welcome.

00:02:34.286 --> 00:02:36.622
Governor DeSantis,
what is the current average age

00:02:36.622 --> 00:02:38.257
of the U.S. Senate?

00:02:38.257 --> 00:02:39.859
-Stone-cold dead.

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.693
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.693 --> 00:02:45.798
-Governor Christie, why do you
want to become president?

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:49.269
-To defeat Hitler.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:50.803
-We already defeated Hitler.

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.107
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.143 --> 00:02:59.846
Mr. Ramaswamy, this next
question is about health care.

00:02:59.846 --> 00:03:02.848
What are your four favorite
euphemisms for sex?

00:03:02.848 --> 00:03:05.818
-Drill. Frack. Burn coal.
Embrace nuclear.

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.720
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:16.329
-You know, in high school,
I never got to embrace nuclear.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:18.131
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.131 --> 00:03:20.365
Governor DeSantis,
who ya got --

00:03:20.365 --> 00:03:22.768
Streisand or Celine Dion?

00:03:22.768 --> 00:03:24.270
-I will take the Barbs.

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:25.972
[ Laughter ]

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:33.245
-Mr. Ramaswamy,

00:03:33.245 --> 00:03:37.750
if you could time-travel
to any year throughout history,

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:40.019
what years
would you go to visit?

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:43.389
-2018. 2020. 2022.

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.825
-Those are -- It's just, like,
kind of all really recent years,

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:48.361
and I think you're failing
to fully take advantage

00:03:48.361 --> 00:03:50.162
of this hypothetical
opportunity.

00:03:50.162 --> 00:03:52.832
Are there any other years
you'd like the chance

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:54.000
to travel back to?

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.568
-2023.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:57.337
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.275
-I'd like to go back in time
and, uh...

00:04:03.275 --> 00:04:05.111
to when we wrote that one.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:06.412
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.314 --> 00:04:10.783
"It's not gonna work
the way you think!"

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:12.352
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.189 --> 00:04:18.558
Governor Christie, as president,

00:04:18.558 --> 00:04:22.194
why would you bring back
low-rise jeans?

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:24.464
-To Increase
American naval power.

00:04:24.464 --> 00:04:26.032
[ Laughter ]

00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.070
-That's great.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.005
Senator Scott, the Actor's Guild

00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:36.075
finally settled their strike
after 118 days.

00:04:36.075 --> 00:04:38.911
And picketing tips
for the next time

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:40.446
so it doesn't last so long?

00:04:40.446 --> 00:04:42.582
-You have to strike in Iran

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.784
if you want to
make a difference.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:47.519
[ Laughter ]

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:49.989
-That one actually went
exactly how I thought it would.

00:04:49.989 --> 00:04:51.958
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:55.828
Governor DeSantis,
you got a lot of heat

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:57.963
for eating pudding
with your fingers,

00:04:57.963 --> 00:05:00.800
but that's the only thing
you eat in a weird way, right?

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:02.568
Like, how do you eat
an ice-cream cone?

00:05:02.568 --> 00:05:04.403
-You gotta work
from the bottom up.

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:08.808
-So weird.
He's such a weird dude.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:12.177
Mr. Ramaswamy, my 7-year-old son
wants to look cooler at school.

00:05:12.177 --> 00:05:14.814
Any advice?
-I would tell him to smoke.

00:05:14.814 --> 00:05:17.583
-Okay.

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:19.719
Governor Christie,
how would you describe

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:21.921
the Charmin Bears?
-A terrorist group

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.490
that has committed to wiping.

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.292
[ Laughter ]

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:33.166
A lot of them
end their sentences weird.

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.867
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:38.303
You know what I mean? Like...

00:05:38.303 --> 00:05:41.273
Like there's another word.
I don't know.

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:43.242
Ambassador Haley,
what do you call it

00:05:43.242 --> 00:05:45.478
when someone shows a little skin

00:05:45.478 --> 00:05:48.380
in exchange
for some free body art?

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:49.682
-Tit for tat.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:51.250
[ Laughter ]

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:58.056
-Governor DeSantis,
what did your wife say

00:05:58.056 --> 00:06:01.227
when she saw all the credit-card
charges for heel lifts?

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:03.029
-"I'm canceling your visa."

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.730
[ Laughter ]

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:06.899
-Mr. Ramaswamy, I heard
you released a new fragrance.

00:06:06.899 --> 00:06:08.000
What's it called?

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.103
-Sexual responsibility for men.

00:06:11.103 --> 00:06:12.972
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.307 --> 00:06:15.675
-Hey.

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:18.977
Hey, Governor Christie.
Check it out.

00:06:18.977 --> 00:06:21.213
I found a dollar lying
over by the vending machines.

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:23.882
-Shame on you. You shouldn't
be taking the money.

00:06:23.882 --> 00:06:26.885
-Geez. It's --
It's just a dollar.

00:06:26.885 --> 00:06:29.922
-I find that
morally reprehensible.

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:32.358
-You okay, buddy?
-I'm tired.

00:06:32.358 --> 00:06:34.193
[ Laughter ]

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.394
-I get it.

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:36.828
Hey, Mr. Ramaswamy,

00:06:36.828 --> 00:06:39.365
how many Adderalls did you take
before this debate?

00:06:39.365 --> 00:06:40.700
-Thousands!

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:42.134
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:43.803
-Senator Scott,

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:47.240
where do you think
my childhood dog is right now?

00:06:47.240 --> 00:06:49.675
-A farm in Iowa.

00:06:49.675 --> 00:06:51.344
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:54.046
-Thanks.

00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:01.454
Governor DeSantis!
Governor Haley!

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:03.922
Starts saying numbers of ships!
Go!

00:07:03.922 --> 00:07:06.391
-355 ships.
-350 ships.

00:07:06.458 --> 00:07:08.461
-385 ships.
-400 ships.

00:07:08.527 --> 00:07:09.895
-600 ships.

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:11.197
-Good job!

00:07:11.197 --> 00:07:12.698
-Over 700 --

00:07:12.698 --> 00:07:15.334
-Stop it, Ron!

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:18.304
We're done with ship numbers!
Okay?!

00:07:18.304 --> 00:07:22.942
That bit is over,
and you ruined it! "700."

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:25.545
Where would you even park
700 ships?

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.081
[ Laughter ]

00:07:35.654 --> 00:07:38.190
Governor Christie,
what does eating at Chipotle

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:40.059
do to people's
lower G.I. system?

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:43.228
-It creates greater unrest
in the entire region.

00:07:43.228 --> 00:07:45.397
-Hm.

00:07:45.397 --> 00:07:47.700
Mr. Ramaswamy,
you seem upset with me.

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:50.069
Do you think someone else
should be moderating
this debate instead?

00:07:50.069 --> 00:07:53.238
-This should be Tucker Carlson,
Joe Rogan, and Elon Musk.

00:07:53.238 --> 00:07:56.041
We'd have 10 times
the viewership, asking questions

00:07:56.041 --> 00:07:58.911
that GOP primary voters
actually care about.

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:00.345
-Okay. Good idea.

00:08:00.345 --> 00:08:03.315
Let's let Elon Musk ask
a question and see how it goes.

00:08:03.315 --> 00:08:05.284
-[ Chuckles ]
Are you a mushroom?

00:08:05.284 --> 00:08:08.087
Do you like being in the dark
and feasting on dead --

00:08:08.087 --> 00:08:10.356
dead plant and animal matter?

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.957
-Alright.

00:08:11.957 --> 00:08:15.328
Would anyone like to respond
to Mr. Musk's terrific question?

00:08:22.134 --> 00:08:23.903
Governor DeSantis, you look like

00:08:23.903 --> 00:08:25.404
you have something
you want to say to Elon.

00:08:25.404 --> 00:08:26.705
-You should not have money.

00:08:26.705 --> 00:08:29.542
-Ambassador Haley.

00:08:29.542 --> 00:08:31.677
Ambassador Haley,
what's the best place

00:08:31.677 --> 00:08:33.813
to fart on an airplane?

00:08:33.813 --> 00:08:37.016
-We have to go and start
beefing up the middle class.

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:39.151
[ Laughter ]

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.887
-Just call it "coach."

00:08:41.887 --> 00:08:45.191
Mr. Ramaswamy, what method would
you use to assassinate Grimace?

00:08:45.191 --> 00:08:46.725
-Fentanyl in a Big Mac.

00:08:46.725 --> 00:08:49.595
-Governor DeSantis,
you look miserable.

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:51.130
Do you even
want to be president?

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.332
-I just want
to get back to Florida.

00:08:53.332 --> 00:08:55.200
-Yeah.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.535
-Governor Christie,

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:58.570
what's the wildest thing
you did in college?

00:08:58.570 --> 00:08:59.705
-Foursome.

00:08:59.705 --> 00:09:01.807
-Well...it looks like
we're out of time,

00:09:01.807 --> 00:09:04.310
so on behalf of the candidates,
have a good night.

00:09:04.310 --> 00:09:06.846
We'll be right back
with our friend Ed Helms.

